{"images":["data:image/webp;base64,"],"messages":[{"content":"<image>\nGraph 3 shows the number of injuries and illnesses a corporation reported per 100 full-time workers from 2003 to 2011. The solid line is the regression line for the data. The dotted line connects the points for 2003 and 2011; it represents the average rate of change in reported injuries and illness over the eight-year period. <image 1> The least-squares regression line is least successful at predicting the number of injury and illness reports in ____________.\nOptions: A: 2003, B: 2005, C: 2007, D: 2009\nAnswer with the option's letter from the given choices directly","role":"user"}]}